Sun Oct 11 19:25:22 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- New package gridcraft 0.5.0 (upstream tag v0.5.0, 2026-10-10):
  native spreadsheet opening and saving .xlsx workbooks and CSV/TSV,
  with hundreds of worksheet functions, formatting, sorting, filtering
  and charts; every action is also runnable headless via gridcraft-cli.
- Highlights: ODS and XLSB import (data plus cached values); charts
  with smooth curves, row/column switching and combo/stock/histogram
  kinds; interface language follows the system (Portuguese, Simplified
  Chinese, Korean, Russian added) with CJK/Thai/Hebrew rendering;
  sheet protection enforces locked cells and keeps hidden formulas
  hidden; Paste Special, Text to Columns and in-cell pictures.
- Excel parity fixes: DATE(1900,2,29) serial, 15-digit ROUND,
  SUMIF/AVERAGEIF range sizing, spill (#SPILL!/#CALC!) handling.
- License derived over the vendor tree for the shipped targets
  (gridcraft, gridcraft-cli): no copyleft linked; tag covers the
  embedded OFL-1.1/Ubuntu-font-1.0 fonts and Unicode-3.0 code, see
  the Legal-Review-Notice in the spec. No vendor/ upstream, so the
  cargo_vendor service runs with update=true (14 crates refreshed).
- Split out gridcraft-cli subpackage (own description and files,
  main package ships the GUI only, main Recommends: gridcraft-cli);
  the headless CLI needs none of the X11/Wayland/Vulkan Requires.

